      "text": "1504\nIEEE/ACM TRANSACTIONS ON AUDIO, SPEECH, AND LANGUAGE PROCESSING, VOL. 28, 2020\nAlthough we evaluate our method on a speaker-dependent\ndataset, the proposed method can be extended to speaker- inde-\npendent speech enhancement as well. It is because the generative\nvocoder can model hundreds of unique voices, and the mapping-\nbased enhancement methods can be speaker- independent as\nwell. In future studies, we will devote efforts to extending\nthe proposed method to speaker-independent application and\nevaluating the speaker generalization.\nACKNOWLEDGMENT\nWe would like to thank Sang-gil Lee for the discussion\nof Flowavenet and Shiliang Zhang for the help of evaluating\nthe speech distortion. We also would like to thank the anony-\nmous reviewers for their constructive comments. The work was\nperformed while the ﬁrst author was an internship at Elevoc\nTechnology Co., Ltd., ShenZhen, China.",
